<title>BELGIUM: EU to discuss MFN sugar imports.</title>
<headline>EU to discuss MFN sugar imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will on Wednesday discuss a most-favoured-nation (MFN) raw cane sugar import quota for 1997, EU member state officials said.</p>
<p>The quota, amounting to some 22,000 tonnes of white sugar equivalent, compensates Finland's traditional suppliers under the former General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT) for trade losses after it joined the EU in 1995.</p>
<p>It includes suppliers such as Cuba and Brazil.</p>
</text>
